{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>יערף</b> Twice in the Masorah. One is here. And the other: יערוף מזבחותם ישודד מצבותם. One who is worthy and learns Torah like Moses, it becomes for him an elixir of life. That is יערף כמטר. And the translation of Onkelos for יערף: יבסם. One who is not worthy, who learned not for its own sake, it becomes for him an elixir of death. That is יערוף מזבחותם. Which is an expression of decapitation, like וערפו שם את העגלה." "<b>לקחי</b> Three times in the Masorah. One is here. And the others: לקחי נא לי פת לחם. זך לקחי. Here it speaks of Torah, for לקח is nothing but Torah, as it says כי לקח טוב נתתי לכם. And this is what they said: if there is no flour, there is no Torah." "<b>יערף כמטר לקחי</b> When? זך לקחי. לקחי לי פת לחם, and this is flour: if there is flour, there is Torah." "<b>לקחי</b> In gematria: קמח." "<b>כטל</b> Twice in the Masorah: תזל כטל. אהיה כטל לישראל. To teach that the Torah is like dew — for Israel specifically. But for the nations, the reverse, as written ראה ויתר גוים, that from Sinai He loosened them, etc." "<b>כמטר</b> כטל. כשעירים. כרביבים. Four expressions corresponding to four traits in learners. And so in the hand of each and every one of Israel, four times. As stated in Eruvin regarding how the order of the Mishnah was arranged: וכרביבים עלי עשב."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:17.645983851Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}